item+ const src/schema.rs :: CLAIM_BEARING_REQUIRED :: pub const CLAIM_BEARING_REQUIRED: [&str; 2] = ["asserts", "contradicts"]; :: Edge types whose existence asserts something about the world (SPEC §5.1). A claim-bearing edge MUST carry exactly one status/basis pair and a real evidence pointer. `derived_from` MAY carry the pair (a claim's provenance is assayable); all other types MUST NOT carry it — a structural edge omits the pair rather than decorating itself with an assay it does not need (SPEC §2.2). :: doc comment :: 44 :: 1
item+ const src/schema.rs :: EDGE_TYPES :: pub const EDGE_TYPES: [&str; 9] = [ :: Edge types (SPEC §1.3). Every type below already exists in a seed corpus. `made` is NOT an edge type: it is attribution recorded on a work's scroll (SPEC §1.2), because there is no person node for the edge to leave from. :: doc comment :: 21 :: 1
item+ const src/schema.rs :: NODE_KINDS :: pub const NODE_KINDS: [&str; 8] = [ :: Node kinds (SPEC §1.2). Eight kinds, each supplied by a seed corpus. There is deliberately no `person` kind: KGOAT is for ideas, not people (D6, SPEC §5.2). A scroll claiming kind `person` is non-conformant. :: doc comment :: 9 :: 1
